# Dataset

The dataset used in this research is a synthetic digital payment transaction dataset created for experimental evaluation of the FraudFusion++ framework.

It was designed to simulate transaction patterns relevant to digital payment fraud detection and to evaluate the performance of the proposed hybrid framework.

The dataset does not contain real customer, financial, or personally identifiable information.

## Purpose

The dataset is used to:

* Train and evaluate the machine learning models.
* Identify anomalous transaction behaviour using Isolation Forest.
* Perform fraud classification using CatBoost.
* Evaluate the risk assessment process of the Adaptive Risk Decision Engine (ARDE).

## Dataset Availability

The dataset is provided in this repository for research and experimental purposes.
